### 3. **Custom Metrics with Lua**
Since you are using Lua for the token bucket implementation, you can also emit custom metrics from your Lua script. These metrics can be collected by Prometheus or another monitoring tool.

#### Emit Custom Metrics
Modify your Lua script to emit custom metrics:

```lua
-- token_bucket.lua
local token_bucket = {}

function token_bucket.new(config)
    local self = {
        capacity = config.capacity,
        fill_rate = config.fill_rate,
        tokens = config.capacity,
        last_check = ngx.now(),
    }
    return setmetatable(self, { __index = token_bucket })
end

function token_bucket:refill()
    local now = ngx.now()
    local elapsed = now - self.last_check
    self.tokens = math.min(self.tokens + elapsed * self.fill_rate, self.capacity)
    self.last_check = now
end

function token_bucket:consume(tokens)
    self:refill()
    if self.tokens >= tokens then
        self.tokens = self.tokens - tokens
        ngx.var.prometheus_metric = "token_bucket_consumed{status=\"success\"} 1"
        return true
    else
        ngx.var.prometheus_metric = "token_bucket_consumed{status=\"failure\"} 1"
        return false
    end
end

return token_bucket
```

